---
title: Configuration File
description: Reference for the most important settings in FOSSBilling's config.php file.
---

Your `config.php` file is in the installation root. This page covers the settings administrators most commonly change. For the full reference, see the [example config](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/main/src/config-sample.php).

## Configuration Options

### Security Settings

These settings control HTTPS and session handling. See [Securing FOSSBilling](/security/securing-fossbilling/#security-options) for production guidance.

| Setting | Default | Description |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| `security.mode` | `strict` | `strict` sets `SameSite=Strict` on session cookies. Both `strict` and `regular` set `HttpOnly`. |
| `security.force_https` | `true` | Redirect HTTP requests to HTTPS and mark session cookies as secure. |
| `security.session_lifespan` | `7200` | Session duration in seconds (2 hours by default). |
| `security.session_regeneration_grace_period` | `300` | Time in seconds that the previous session ID can still be used after regeneration. |
| `security.perform_session_fingerprinting` | `true` | Verify browser fingerprint on each request to help prevent session hijacking. |
| `security.debug_fingerprint` | `false` | Log fingerprint checks for debugging (enable temporarily only). |

### Trusted Proxies

Configure reverse-proxy support so FOSSBilling correctly detects the visitor's IP and protocol:

```php
'security' => [
    'trusted_proxies' => [
        'enabled' => false,
        'proxies' => [],
        'headers' => 'x_forwarded',
    ],
],
```

| Setting | Default | Description |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| `trusted_proxies.enabled` | `false` | Enable trusted proxy detection |
| `trusted_proxies.proxies` | `[]` | List of trusted proxy IPs or CIDR ranges |
| `trusted_proxies.headers` | `x_forwarded` | Header type: `x_forwarded` (standard) or `forwarded` (RFC 7239) |

See [Reverse Proxies](/security/securing-fossbilling/#reverse-proxies) for installer detection and HTTPS forwarding.

### Encryption Key

- `salt` — Used for reversible encryption. **Keep this secret and don't change it** after installation.

### URLs

- `url` — Your FOSSBilling URL with trailing slash (e.g., `https://billing.example.com/`).
- `admin_area_prefix` — Admin panel path (default: `/admin`)

### Debugging

These settings are in the `debug_and_monitoring` array in `config.php`.

- `debug` — Show detailed error messages. **Disable in production.**
- `log_stacktrace` — Log exception stack traces when debug mode is enabled.
- `stacktrace_length` — Maximum number of frames in each logged stack trace.
- `report_errors` — Set to `true` to enable automated error reporting or `false` to disable it.

### Updates

- `update_branch` — Which updates to receive:
  - `"release"` — Stable releases only (recommended for production)
  - `"preview"` — Development builds (may have bugs)

### Maintenance Mode

Temporarily disable public access. Use `allowed_urls` for endpoints that must stay reachable and `allowed_ips` for trusted networks that should bypass maintenance mode.

```php
'maintenance_mode' => [
    'enabled' => true,
    'allowed_urls' => ['/api/guest/*'],
    'allowed_ips' => ['192.168.1.0/24'],
],
```

### Cron Settings

- `disable_auto_cron` — Disable automatic cron execution when admins log in

### Localization

| Setting | Default | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| `i18n.locale` | `en_US` | Default language code |
| `i18n.timezone` | `UTC` | Default timezone |
| `i18n.date_format` | `medium` | Options: `none`, `short`, `medium`, `long` |
| `i18n.time_format` | `short` | Options: `none`, `short`, `medium`, `long` |
| `i18n.datetime_pattern` | — | Custom date/time pattern |
| `i18n.auto_detect_locale` | `true` | Automatically detect visitor's preferred language from browser settings |

### Data & Logging

`path_data` sets the directory for application data, including cache files and logs.

### Database

```php
'db' => [
    'driver' => 'pdo_mysql',
    'host' => '127.0.0.1',
    'port' => '3306',
    'name' => 'fossbilling',
    'user' => 'fossbilling_user',
    'password' => 'your_password',
],
```

### Twig (Templates)

| Setting | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `twig.debug` | Enable Twig debug mode |
| `twig.auto_reload` | Auto-reload templates on changes |
| `twig.cache` | Template cache directory |

### API Settings

Control API access.

- Use `require_referrer_header` to lock browser-originated requests to your install URL, and `allowed_ips` for explicit allowlists.
- Keep `CSRFPrevention` enabled. The bundled [JavaScript API wrapper](/extensions-and-development/javascript/) handles CSRF tokens for session-authenticated browser calls.

```php
'api' => [
    'require_referrer_header' => false,
    'allowed_ips' => [],
    'CSRFPrevention' => true,
],
```

### Rate Limiter

| Setting | Default | Description |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| `rate_limiter.enabled` | `true` | Enable rate limiting. |
| `rate_limiter.whitelist_ips` | `[]` | IP addresses or CIDR ranges exempt from rate limiting. |
| `rate_limiter.policies` | `[]` | Overrides for individual built-in policies. |

Set only the fields you want to override. This example lowers the `client_signup` limit from five to three attempts per hour. [Built-in rate-limiter policies](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/FOSSBilling/Security/RateLimiter.php#L42-L79) · [Symfony rate limiter documentation](https://symfony.com/doc/current/rate_limiter.html)

```php
'rate_limiter' => [
    'policies' => [
        'client_signup' => ['limit' => 3],
    ],
],
```

## Environment Variables

Some settings can be overridden via environment variables:

```bash
APP_ENV=dev        # Enable development mode
APP_DEBUG=true     # Enable debug mode
DB_HOST=db.example.com   # Override database host
DB_NAME=fossbilling      # Override database name
DB_USER=myuser           # Override database user
DB_PASS=mypass           # Override database password
DB_PORT=3306             # Override database port
```

## Making Changes

{% steps %}
1. Edit `config.php` with a text editor
2. Save the file
3. Clear the cache: **System → Tools → Clear cache** (or delete `/data/cache/`)
4. Test your changes
{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" %}
Always back up `config.php` before making changes. A syntax error will break your installation.
{% /aside %}
